quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  67,27,"But when they shall see it quite near, the faces of the disbelievers will become darkened (and deformed), and it will be said (to them): ‘This is what you were calling for.’"
  67,28,"Say: ‘Tell me, whether Allah destroys me and those with me or shows mercy to us, but who will shelter the disbelievers from a painful punishment?’"
  67,29,"Say: ‘He is the Most-Compassionate (Lord); we believe in Him, and upon Him do we trust. You will soon know who is in obvious error.’"
  67,30,"Say: ‘Tell me, if your water were to sink deep (into the earth), then who would bring you flowing water?’"
  68,1,"Nun. By the pen, and whatever they (the angels) write down!"
  68,2,"(O Prophet!) By the Grace of your Lord, you are not insane."
  68,3,"And most surely, you shall have an unceasing reward."
  68,4,"And indeed, you are upon an exalted moral character."
  68,5,"You will see, and they will see,"
  68,6,which one of you is afflicted (with madness).
  68,7,"Indeed, your Lord knows best who strays from His way, and He knows best who are rightly guided."
  68,8,So do not yield to the deniers.
  68,9,They wish you to compromise (with them) so they can compromise (with you).
  68,10,"So do not listen to any disgraceful swearer,"
  68,11,"(or to any) defamer (and slanderer), scandalmonger, mischief spreader (and backbiter),"
  68,12,"(or) forbidder of the good, sinful transgressor,"
  68,13,"(or) ignoble, and on top of that, baseborn (i.e. an illegitimate child),"
  68,14,simply because he has wealth and children.
  68,15,"When Our Verses are recited to him, he says: ‘(These are) the fictitious stories of the ancients.’"
